;; A query's `:expect` lists its projection classes — the goal's atoms under
;; its rows (M1e2 S1e2.1a.5, `region_language.md` § 5) — so a listed fact the
;; goal does not match is not a class of it. A claim about the state, which
;; `(q A H1)` here would be, is the region claim's, `(solve … :expect (region
;; …))`. Until the switch this was M1c's rule 1, *the goal's relations are
;; mandatory*, and the same file was refused for naming `q` and not `p`.

(relation p Thing Place)
(relation q Thing Place)
(p A H1)
(q A H1)
(query :goal (p A ?h) :expect (model (q A H1)))
